[Music]  this week we  naturally provide you with another  original episode  this time it's about one of the most  popular animation franchises of recent  years  namely how to train your dragon after  three  hugely successful movies the last of  which was released in 2019  there is unfortunately no fourth part in  sight today  we talk about how likely it seems that a  fourth part will be released after all  and what it could be  about so have fun with our newest video  first we'll recap the storyline from  parts one two three to bring you up to  date  in the first part from 2010 we dive into  the world of the viking offspring hiccup  in contrast to his comrades hiccup is  very dainty and has little in common  with a fearsome  viking just like his father the  chieftain stoick hiccup has the desire  to kill a dragon  as the viking village is suddenly  attacked by dragons young hiccup is  given the chance to prove to his father  and everyone else  exactly what he's capable of at first he  succeeds in shooting down  a night fury a particular dangerous  species against the old viking tradition  however the two become  friends and hiccup's life is turned  completely upside down  finally the fight between dragons and  villagers is proclaimed to be over  and both sides live peacefully with each  other from then on  in part 2 from 2014 hiccup and toothless  as he names his dragon have been friends  for 5 years  during one of the many exploratory  adventures they come across a mystical  ice cave  populated by many dragons and especially  the legendary dragon rider  it eventually turns out that the masked  rider is hiccup's mother who was  believed dead  and that she lives among the dragons  here exploring the actually peaceful  beasts  the unscrupulous drago bloodthis who  fears nothing sees things differently  and wants to train the dragons for his  army in the end the conflict ends mildly  for the villagers as dragon loses  control of his army and has to flee  hiccup is appointed chieftain due to his  outstanding achievements and the village  is rebuilt part 3 was released in 2019  and continues the story of the previous  ones  hiccup and his girlfriend astrid take  care of the day-to-day business in burke  while toothless has risen to become the  leader of the dragon colony  the piece does not last for long of  course since a new threat looms  on the one hand a light fury enters the  life of toothless on the other hand the  evil dragon hunter grimmle is after the  dragon leader  the solution to the problem is to  discover the so-called secret world  where the dragons can live in peace  after a difficult confrontation with  dremel and the discovery of the secret  world  the alpha dragon toothless finally  manages to lead his fellow dragons to  the secret world  hiccup and astrid's personal happiness  also flourishes more than  ever as the two married the following  winter after settling down on the new  island  the film series ends with hiccup and his  family flying away on toothless in  stormfly  and his voice off screen saying that he  wants to keep the dragon's existence a  secret  until humanity is mature enough for them  to coexist peacefully  in addition to the three main films  there's also this small but  nice christmas special called how to  train your dragon homecoming from  the story revolves around the now  significantly aged spouses astrid  and hiccup and their two children zephyr  and nothing they're all preparing for  snuggle talk which is a big family  celebration with plenty of presents  hidden in the vikings helmets  over the course of the 22-minute  spin-off father hiccup tells his  children how important peace with the  dragons is  and as if by magic hiccup's old  companion toothless appears to share one  last great adventure  and to reminisce with his former master  before we discuss a potential plot for a  fourth part it should be said that  director dean de blah has already  clarified several times that no  fourth part is planned and that the  third part has already completed the  storyline  many fans were hoping that the  relatively large time jump at the end of  how the training dragon 3 would make  room for more content  and this is where the older hiccup and  the older toothless are united with the  families  the 22 minute christmas special on how  to train your dragon homecoming also  makes you long for more as even the  story of part 3 somewhat continued there  in our opinion there are 4 possibilities  for a continuation of the how to train  your dragon series  on the one side there could of course be  a direct sequel to part 3 in terms of  content  for example the plot could be said after  this special homecoming  and tell a final story of hiccup and  toothless do  would likely have another exciting  adventure but ultimately such a sequel  would probably feel  very repetitive and unnecessary the  ending of part 3 fits wonderfully with  the conclusion to the film series  and is a successful ending for both the  fans and the studio  thus a seamless sequel is the most  unrealistic scenario in our opinion  the second possibility would be a story  of hiccup's children nothing and zephyr  they could have reached teenage or  adulthood after a time jump and follow  in their father's footsteps  for instance two parallel stories of the  siblings existence could be told and the  story could eventually be brought  together  besides the aged characters from the  previous three parts new characters  could be introduced without losing the  charm of the original  the main problem at this point is that  hiccup simply cannot be left  out of the main role and that overall we  know far too little about the children  in addition the time jump that would be  necessary from part 3 to part 4  would probably feel kind of odd given  that the parts before only covered a  period of few years  something we also consider possible is a  prequel that takes place before the  first part  this third scenario is not unlikely  especially because  neither the universe know the characters  would have to be changed  they could for example focus on life  before hiccup's birth or tell the story  of the village of burke thus  show the audience a bit more of the  truly  lovingly designed world as a fourth and  final option  we also envision one or more spin-offs  in any case the film universe has enough  interesting side characters  stories about the former lives of  hiccup's parents astrid or  of course toothless come to mind in the  case of the latter for example they  could tell us how the dragon got to  burke in the first place and how he  became the dragon he is  we definitely think this is the most  likely option partly due to the fact  that this scenario offers a  lot more creative possibilities the  fourth scenario is also supported by the  fact that director de bla already wrote  of the rest in 2014  things would be different with spin-offs  of course since the original by author  cressida cowell also consists of 12  books hence the franchise is far from  dead but it's highly unlikely that fans  can expect a seamless follow-up in the  form of a possible part 4.  now naturally we are interested in your  opinion how likely do you think the  sequel to the how to train your dragon  series is  and which scenario would you prefer feel  free to leave your thoughts in the  comments section below and  if you like the latest original be sure  to subscribe and leave us a like  see you next time  [Music]  bye

